# CWYD-12 — traces of chat and ingestion in Jaeger (DOM-22..24).
# Setup, in .env: OTEL_TRACES_EXPORTER=otlp (keep CAPTURE_CONTENT=false), then
#   docker compose --profile observability up --build --wait
# Jaeger UI: http://localhost:16686 → Service "cwyd-backend".
# Find a question's trace: Tags `app.request_id=<request_id from the response>`.
# Find an ingestion's trace: Tags `app.document.id=<id from the upload response>`.
# Screenshots: docs/evidence/CWYD-12/ (ingest, answered, refused, failed).
# REST Client (VS Code / Cursor) or JetBrains HTTP Client, from the repository root.

# From inside the dev container set @host = host.docker.internal.
@host = localhost
@api = http://{{host}}:8000

### 1. Ingestion trace: 202 + `id`. Jaeger: `POST /documents` → fastapi.background_task →
### `ingest.document` → ingest.parse, ingest.chunk, ingest.embed, ingest.store;
### ingest.document ends with app.document.status=ready. ingest.embed carries
### gen_ai.response.model, gen_ai.usage.input_tokens and app.cost.usd (CWYD-28), and
### `docker compose logs backend` shows "Indexed document <id>: N chunks, T embedding tokens,
### estimated cost C USD" (ids and numbers only).
### (Already uploaded? 200 with the existing document and no new trace: DOM-04.)
POST {{api}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cwyd

--cwyd
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="parental-leave-policy.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ../../backend/tests/fixtures/documents/parental-leave-policy.md
--cwyd--

### 2. Sourced answer: 200 outcome "answered"; header X-Request-ID = body request_id.
### Jaeger: `POST /chat` → fastapi.endpoint → `rag.chat` → retrieval.embed_query,
### retrieval.hybrid, answer_generation (+ rerank with RERANK_ENABLED=true).
### rag.chat: app.outcome=answered, gen_ai.request.model,
### gen_ai.usage.input_tokens / output_tokens (all model calls, the query embedding
### included; retrieval.embed_query has its own model and tokens), app.answer.sources,
### app.cost.usd (absent if a model is not in backend/app/prices.yaml).
### Retrieved vs used chunks: app.retrieval.returned / app.retrieval.evidence on
### retrieval.hybrid, app.context.chunks on answer_generation.
### No question, chunk or answer text in any attribute.
POST {{api}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "What is the monthly coworking reimbursement limit?"}

### 3. Refusal: 200 outcome "insufficient_evidence". Jaeger: app.outcome=refused; with no
### evidence past the relevance gate there is no answer_generation span (no chat call), and
### rag.chat's tokens and app.cost.usd are the query embedding's only (CWYD-28).
POST {{api}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "What is the capital of Australia?"}

### 4. Provider failure: set CHAT_MODEL=claude-does-not-exist (or gpt-does-not-exist) in .env,
### `docker compose --profile observability up -d backend`, send this request, then restore
### CHAT_MODEL. Expect 502 {"code": "chat_unavailable", "detail": ..., "request_id": ...}.
### Jaeger: answer_generation and rag.chat with error status, error.type=ChatModelUnavailable,
### app.outcome=error, and no exception message or stack trace on the spans.
POST {{api}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "What is the monthly coworking reimbursement limit?"}

### 5. Every response carries X-Request-ID, errors carry it in the body too: 400
### {"code": "empty_question", ..., "request_id": ...}.
POST {{api}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "   "}
